DISPATCH_LINE(tutorial_garage, tutorial_garage_1, "The runner's first shift began in a garage. The door at the back opened onto another world.")
DISPATCH_LINE(tutorial_garage, tutorial_garage_2, "Between a stack of pizza boxes and the portal stood the newest member of the salvage trade.")
DISPATCH_LINE(tutorial_garage, tutorial_garage_3, "It was a small garage for a company with so much floor space on the other side.")
DISPATCH_LINE(tutorial_garage, tutorial_garage_4, "This side of the doorway was home. The runner's wages lay somewhere on the other side.")
DISPATCH_LINE(tutorial_garage, tutorial_garage_5, "A pallet, a portal, an empty garage. The runner's employers had kept the overhead low.")
DISPATCH_LINE(tutorial_haul, tutorial_haul_1, "Three pieces of salvage would fill the order. The first lay just past the portal.")
DISPATCH_LINE(tutorial_haul, tutorial_haul_2, "Out on the carpet lay the first delivery. Its destination was a pallet back in the garage.")
DISPATCH_LINE(tutorial_haul, tutorial_haul_3, "Every piece they brought back belonged on the pallet. Three trips would do it.")
DISPATCH_LINE(tutorial_haul, tutorial_haul_4, "The runner had a modest assignment. Three finds on the garage pallet before the shift was out.")
DISPATCH_LINE(tutorial_haul, tutorial_haul_5, "The order called for three pieces. Beyond the doorway, even a lamp tube was worth bringing home.")
DISPATCH_LINE(tutorial_core, tutorial_core_1, "Three boxes sat on the pallet. Beyond them, something else had begun to glow.")
DISPATCH_LINE(tutorial_core, tutorial_core_2, "The order was complete. The bright return on the scanner had an appeal all its own.")
DISPATCH_LINE(tutorial_core, tutorial_core_3, "There was the last of the salvage, bright enough to find its own way home.")
DISPATCH_LINE(tutorial_core, tutorial_core_4, "The runner had one more thing to carry back. It cast a light of its own.")
DISPATCH_LINE(tutorial_core, tutorial_core_5, "After three ordinary deliveries came a rather extraordinary one. The core was waiting.")
DISPATCH_LINE(accident, accident_1, "For a moment there was nothing but white. Where the way home had been, there was a wall.")
DISPATCH_LINE(accident, accident_2, "The core reached the doorway. The garage and the runner parted company.")
DISPATCH_LINE(accident, accident_3, "A flash swallowed the portal. For the stranded crew, home was now a machine on tracks.")
DISPATCH_LINE(accident, accident_4, "The doorway left a burnt outline. It was a poor substitute for a way home.")
DISPATCH_LINE(accident, accident_5, "A moment ago the garage had been a step away. The runner would have to take the long way now.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_stalker, first_stalker_1, "The runner had spotted a stalker. It could wait all night for someone to look away.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_stalker, first_stalker_2, "A stalker had come into view. Its chance would come when nobody was looking.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_stalker, first_stalker_3, "There was one thing a stalker couldn't do. It couldn't take a step while someone watched.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_stalker, first_stalker_4, "As long as the creature stayed in sight, the runner could back away. Stalkers had rules.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_stalker, first_stalker_5, "In the dark, a glance alone wouldn't hold a stalker. The runner's beam could.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_crawler, first_crawler_1, "A crawler had found the hall. A careless footfall could give it a direction.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_crawler, first_crawler_2, "Blind as it was, the crawler could follow the sound of a sprint. A crouch was quieter.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_crawler, first_crawler_3, "This one hunted by ear. The runner's best chance lay in a quiet pair of shoes.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_crawler, first_crawler_4, "A crawler charged in a straight line. A step to the side could leave it arguing with a wall.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_crawler, first_crawler_5, "To the crawler, a still figure was part of the room. A running one was an address.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_shadow, first_shadow_1, "The shadow recoiled from a glance. A long stare was another matter.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_shadow, first_shadow_2, "A shadow favored anyone who strayed alone. Brief eye contact could send it away.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_shadow, first_shadow_3, "The runner had caught sight of a shadow. Staring would turn its unease into anger.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_shadow, first_shadow_4, "Gone with a glance, furious under a stare. A shadow was particular about being seen.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_shadow, first_shadow_5, "Even a shadow could lose its temper. A beam held on its face would do it.")
DISPATCH_LINE(pickup_clock, pickup_clock_1, "The runner had acquired a clock that kept excellent time, some distance from the truth.")
DISPATCH_LINE(pickup_clock, pickup_clock_2, "Off the wall and into the haul. The clock remained as punctual about being wrong as ever.")
DISPATCH_LINE(pickup_clock, pickup_clock_3, "Somewhere there was a buyer for a clock like this. Presumably an employer.")
DISPATCH_LINE(pickup_clock, pickup_clock_4, "The clock joined the salvage. Whatever hour it kept now belonged to the runner.")
DISPATCH_LINE(pickup_clock, pickup_clock_5, "Nothing was quite on time down here. The wall clock at least was consistent about it.")
DISPATCH_LINE(quota_ready, quota_ready_1, "The fifth lamp came on. Beside the hopper, the descent lever was ready.")
DISPATCH_LINE(quota_ready, quota_ready_2, "That was the quota. One pull of the lever would put the crew on the floor below.")
DISPATCH_LINE(quota_ready, quota_ready_3, "Five little lights. For the runner, they added up to a way off this floor.")
DISPATCH_LINE(quota_ready, quota_ready_4, "The hopper had taken its share. The choice of when to descend now belonged to the crew.")
DISPATCH_LINE(quota_ready, quota_ready_5, "Enough salvage at last. Nothing stood between the rig and the next floor but a lever.")
DISPATCH_LINE(drill_started, drill_started_1, "The lever went down. Under the rig, the floor began to give.")
DISPATCH_LINE(drill_started, drill_started_2, "This time the rumbling belonged to the crew. The drill was cutting a way down.")
DISPATCH_LINE(drill_started, drill_started_3, "The shift was moving downstairs, break room and all.")
DISPATCH_LINE(drill_started, drill_started_4, "There were easier ways to reach the next floor. None of them belonged to the runner.")
DISPATCH_LINE(drill_started, drill_started_5, "So much for this floor. The drill had already begun work on the ceiling of the next.")
DISPATCH_LINE(rig_fault, rig_fault_1, "The engine cut out. Somewhere on the rig, a fault was waiting for a wrench.")
DISPATCH_LINE(rig_fault, rig_fault_2, "The rig had stopped. The cabin light drew on its little reserve of power.")
DISPATCH_LINE(rig_fault, rig_fault_3, "There were three places a repair could be needed. A fuse box and two engine covers.")
DISPATCH_LINE(rig_fault, rig_fault_4, "The machine that kept the hall at a distance had gone quiet. Its reserve wouldn't last.")
DISPATCH_LINE(rig_fault, rig_fault_5, "A breakdown left the crew a little time under the cabin lamp. Then came the dark.")
DISPATCH_LINE(rig_repaired, rig_repaired_1, "The engine caught. The break room was a moving address again.")
DISPATCH_LINE(rig_repaired, rig_repaired_2, "A repair, a shudder, and the rig was back to eating its way through the floor.")
DISPATCH_LINE(rig_repaired, rig_repaired_3, "The runner's shelter made an awful noise. It was good to have that noise back.")
DISPATCH_LINE(rig_repaired, rig_repaired_4, "Power returned to the rig. The halls would have to keep their distance again.")
DISPATCH_LINE(rig_repaired, rig_repaired_5, "The silence ended with a familiar putter. Somebody had earned a seat on the couch.")
DISPATCH_LINE(low_flashlight, low_flashlight_1, "The beam began to blink. The runner was spending the last of the battery.")
DISPATCH_LINE(low_flashlight, low_flashlight_2, "A flicker put a price on every second of light. A spare cell would buy some time.")
DISPATCH_LINE(low_flashlight, low_flashlight_3, "The flashlight had little left. In a powered cabin it could recharge, switched off.")
DISPATCH_LINE(low_flashlight, low_flashlight_4, "The runner's pool of light kept breaking up. The battery was almost spent.")
DISPATCH_LINE(low_flashlight, low_flashlight_5, "A dying flashlight had a way of making the distance back to the rig feel personal.")
DISPATCH_LINE(cabin_recovery, cabin_recovery_1, "Inside the powered cabin, the runner had a chance to mend.")
DISPATCH_LINE(cabin_recovery, cabin_recovery_2, "The break room was a good place to be hurt. In there, a little strength came back.")
DISPATCH_LINE(cabin_recovery, cabin_recovery_3, "There was room for a sore body and a moment's rest aboard the rig.")
DISPATCH_LINE(cabin_recovery, cabin_recovery_4, "For now, the runner had shelter. The powered cabin gave an injury time to ease.")
DISPATCH_LINE(cabin_recovery, cabin_recovery_5, "The rig carried more than a drill. It carried somewhere to recover between trips.")
DISPATCH_LINE(wall_broken, wall_broken_1, "A wall gave way. The sound carried farther than a pair of footsteps ever could.")
DISPATCH_LINE(wall_broken, wall_broken_2, "There was a fresh way through. Its opening had been announced to the whole hall.")
DISPATCH_LINE(wall_broken, wall_broken_3, "Someone had opened the wall. Anyone hunting by ear had a reason to pay attention.")
DISPATCH_LINE(wall_broken, wall_broken_4, "The crew had traded a cracked wall for a passage and a great deal of noise.")
DISPATCH_LINE(wall_broken, wall_broken_5, "A partition came down. Even an empty corridor had plenty to say about that.")
DISPATCH_LINE(study_complete, study_complete_1, "Another species entered the field guide. The crew earned a little money for the entry.")
DISPATCH_LINE(study_complete, study_complete_2, "There was a price on a good look at a creature. The crew had just earned it.")
DISPATCH_LINE(study_complete, study_complete_3, "Fieldwork had paid off. The creature now had a place in the notes and the till.")
DISPATCH_LINE(study_complete, study_complete_4, "That sighting settled an entry in the ledger. A living witness was worth paying.")
DISPATCH_LINE(study_complete, study_complete_5, "The crew had studied something the company could put a name to. It paid for the trouble.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_load, first_load_1, "For the first time this shift, the runner had something to bring back.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_load, first_load_2, "One piece of salvage changed the runner's hands from empty to occupied.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_load, first_load_3, "The scavenger had their first find. Anything else they picked up would add to the weight.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_load, first_load_4, "An empty bag had made for easy walking. The job had other requirements.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_load, first_load_5, "There was salvage in hand at last. The return trip would have a purpose.")
DISPATCH_LINE(cargo_full, cargo_full_1, "Four pieces, four places to carry them. The fifth would take some bargaining.")
DISPATCH_LINE(cargo_full, cargo_full_2, "The runner had filled the last slot. The next find would have to displace an old one.")
DISPATCH_LINE(cargo_full, cargo_full_3, "From here on, picking something up meant deciding what to leave behind.")
DISPATCH_LINE(cargo_full, cargo_full_4, "A full load settled the question of quantity. Four pieces was the limit.")
DISPATCH_LINE(cargo_full, cargo_full_5, "Every carrying slot was spoken for. Even a small prize would need its own space.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_deposit, first_deposit_1, "The first salvage went into the hopper. The gauge began its climb.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_deposit, first_deposit_2, "Every floor asked for a quota. The crew had made its first payment on this one.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_deposit, first_deposit_3, "Something useful disappeared into the rig. The figure on the gauge went up.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_deposit, first_deposit_4, "The hopper took the first delivery. Salvage had bought the crew a little progress.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_deposit, first_deposit_5, "The crew had begun to buy a way down, one piece of salvage at a time.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_wall_door, first_wall_door_1, "A door hung on a blank wall. Someone had taken care to hang it straight.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_wall_door, first_wall_door_2, "Nothing behind the door but wall. The runner had found a job half done in remarkable detail.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_wall_door, first_wall_door_3, "Most doors divided two places. This one seemed content with the one it had.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_wall_door, first_wall_door_4, "There ought to have been a room behind that door. The wall had other ideas.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_wall_door, first_wall_door_5, "The frame was quite convincing. The solid wall behind it spoiled the effect.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_ceiling_stair, first_ceiling_stair_1, "The staircase rose straight into the ceiling. Apparently the upper floor had declined delivery.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_ceiling_stair, first_ceiling_stair_2, "Somebody had built the stairs. Somebody else had finished the ceiling. Both jobs looked complete.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_ceiling_stair, first_ceiling_stair_3, "Each step offered a little more height. The last offered plaster.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_ceiling_stair, first_ceiling_stair_4, "Halfway up, it might have passed for an ordinary staircase. The ceiling gave the game away.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_ceiling_stair, first_ceiling_stair_5, "Above the runner, a staircase and a ceiling had reached a quiet disagreement.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_echo_hall, first_echo_hall_1, "The corridor repeated itself with the care of someone copying a signature.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_echo_hall, first_echo_hall_2, "There was a stretch of hall, then its twin, then much the same stretch again.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_echo_hall, first_echo_hall_3, "A map of this corridor could have been made with a rubber stamp.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_echo_hall, first_echo_hall_4, "The pattern came round again. It was the sort of place that made distance hard to judge.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_echo_hall, first_echo_hall_5, "An office supplier might have called it a repeating unit. A traveler had to walk through every copy.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_chasm, first_chasm_1, "A narrow crossing spanned the chasm. On either side, there was considerably less floor.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_chasm, first_chasm_2, "The gap was wide enough to earn its bridge. The runner could see the way across.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_chasm, first_chasm_3, "On a plan, that bridge would have been a thin line. From here it looked thinner.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_chasm, first_chasm_4, "An office with a chasm through it made an odd address. The bridge was a courtesy.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_chasm, first_chasm_5, "The bridge carried on where the floor gave out. That was all the reassurance on offer.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_twin, first_twin_1, "These rooms ran to doubles. Even the furniture seemed to have been ordered from memory.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_twin, first_twin_2, "Someone had furnished the place twice. The resemblance went well beyond the floor plan.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_twin, first_twin_3, "A familiar arrangement in a second room. It was the little differences that gave it away.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_twin, first_twin_4, "A matching suite made a poor landmark. There was always another room willing to answer to its name.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_twin, first_twin_5, "This room had a twin. Neither looked particularly pleased about the arrangement.")
DISPATCH_LINE(long_walk, long_walk_1, "The runner kept walking. A building of this size could waste a good afternoon one footstep at a time.")
DISPATCH_LINE(long_walk, long_walk_2, "At this pace, a decent pair of shoes counted as company equipment.")
DISPATCH_LINE(long_walk, long_walk_3, "Back home, distance had names. A block, a corner, the way to the store. Here it was mostly footsteps.")
DISPATCH_LINE(long_walk, long_walk_4, "Long stretches like this never made it into the training film. Somebody still had to walk them.")
DISPATCH_LINE(long_walk, long_walk_5, "A map could fold this whole journey into a pocket. The runner had no such luxury.")
DISPATCH_LINE(long_walk, long_walk_6, "For a while, the most interesting sound in the building belonged to a pair of shoes.")
DISPATCH_LINE(long_walk, long_walk_7, "Somewhere there ought to have been a directory. It would have needed a room of its own.")
DISPATCH_LINE(long_walk, long_walk_8, "There were hours of work that produced a crate of salvage. Others merely put miles on a pair of soles.")
DISPATCH_LINE(long_walk, long_walk_9, "So long as the runner kept moving, the place had the decency to look like a route.")
DISPATCH_LINE(long_walk, long_walk_10, "The distance covered would have made a respectable commute. The scenery offered no opinion.")
DISPATCH_LINE(long_walk, long_walk_11, "An empty stretch of building had all the time in the world. The runner spent theirs by the step.")
DISPATCH_LINE(long_walk, long_walk_12, "Ordinary places became familiar with use. This one seemed to get longer.")
DISPATCH_LINE(long_walk, long_walk_13, "A night watchman could wear out a pair of shoes down here without ever catching up on the rounds.")
DISPATCH_LINE(long_walk, long_walk_14, "The runner carried on through space that nobody had thought to give a name.")
DISPATCH_LINE(run_briefing, run_briefing_1, "The runner's job was to feed salvage to the drill. When five lamps lit, the lever would take it down.")
DISPATCH_LINE(run_briefing, run_briefing_2, "The rig took its payment in salvage. A full quota bought the crew a trip to the next floor.")
DISPATCH_LINE(run_briefing, run_briefing_3, "Everything the scavenger hauled to the hopper counted toward descent. The full gauge unlocked the lever.")
DISPATCH_LINE(run_briefing, run_briefing_4, "Each floor named its price in salvage. Once the hopper had enough, the crew could drill down.")
DISPATCH_LINE(run_briefing, run_briefing_5, "The way down ran through the hopper. Enough loot filled the gauge and put the lever in play.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_facewall, first_facewall_1, "The furniture faced the wall. Whatever the room had once been for, it was over.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_facewall, first_facewall_2, "This room had been arranged for an audience with the wallpaper.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_facewall, first_facewall_3, "There was something almost polite about the furniture. It had turned its back.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_facewall, first_facewall_4, "Somebody had taken the trouble to face the furniture toward a perfectly blank wall.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_facewall, first_facewall_5, "The wall had everyone's attention in here. Even the furniture seemed to be waiting.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_vitrine, first_vitrine_1, "Behind the glass stood a furnished room. A person could look right in and still be outside.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_vitrine, first_vitrine_2, "Most windows offered a view of somewhere else. This one offered more office.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_vitrine, first_vitrine_3, "There was a light on in the sealed room. It had been left on for the furniture.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_vitrine, first_vitrine_4, "The room behind the glass had everything an office needed, except a way in.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_vitrine, first_vitrine_5, "The scavenger had found a room arranged for display. The glass made a very firm invitation to look.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_plugged_hall, first_plugged_hall_1, "The corridor came to a solid stop. Its builders had evidently changed their minds.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_plugged_hall, first_plugged_hall_2, "Beyond the plug lay a question best answered from the other side.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_plugged_hall, first_plugged_hall_3, "The hall promised a route and then withdrew the offer.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_plugged_hall, first_plugged_hall_4, "A passage had been sealed here. The runner could follow its intention farther than its floor.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_plugged_hall, first_plugged_hall_5, "The corridor ended in a plug, as though someone had wanted the shape of a way through, but only the shape.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_nested_rooms, first_nested_rooms_1, "Inside the room was another room. Whoever planned the building had packed it very carefully.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_nested_rooms, first_nested_rooms_2, "A room within a room gave the word indoors a second degree.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_nested_rooms, first_nested_rooms_3, "There was an entire interior tucked inside this one. The runner had found the building's parentheses.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_nested_rooms, first_nested_rooms_4, "One enclosure held the next. The floor plan would have looked like a set of packing instructions.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_nested_rooms, first_nested_rooms_5, "Usually a room shared its walls with a neighbor. Here a room had taken one in.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_spiral, first_spiral_1, "The corridor wound inward. Each turn gave away a little more of the building's sense of humor.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_spiral, first_spiral_2, "A spiral was an expensive way to reach the middle of anything. Space was cheap here.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_spiral, first_spiral_3, "The hall kept turning about a center the runner could feel before they could see it.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_spiral, first_spiral_4, "The building had curled a length of corridor into a coil and left it that way.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_spiral, first_spiral_5, "Some passages led from one place to another. This one seemed fascinated by its own middle.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_skywell, first_skywell_1, "A shaft of light reached deep into the building. That was as close as the room came to a sky.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_skywell, first_skywell_2, "Above the runner, the light well gave an ordinary patch of floor a remarkable address.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_skywell, first_skywell_3, "All that height, just to deliver a little light. For once the building had been generous.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_skywell, first_skywell_4, "The ceiling rose around a well of light. Below it, the runner might almost have been outdoors.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_skywell, first_skywell_5, "Light had found its own route into the concourse. It traveled considerably lighter than the scavenger.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_basin, first_basin_1, "The floor sank into a dry basin. There was a way down on foot.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_basin, first_basin_2, "A depression opened below the usual floor level. Even the low ground had an address down here.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_basin, first_basin_3, "There was a basin where a level floor might reasonably have been expected. Its bottom could be reached.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_basin, first_basin_4, "The building dipped here. A runner could walk down into the hollow and still be indoors.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_basin, first_basin_5, "From above it looked like missing floor. Farther down, the basin supplied its own.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_dark_wing, first_dark_wing_1, "The runner had found a dark wing. There was very little to tell one corner from the next.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_dark_wing, first_dark_wing_2, "The building spent plenty on lighting. This stretch had apparently missed its turn.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_dark_wing, first_dark_wing_3, "A whole part of the floor lay dark. The darkness fitted the rooms exactly.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_dark_wing, first_dark_wing_4, "Light gave the usual landmarks their shape. In this wing, the shapes were harder to come by.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_dark_wing, first_dark_wing_5, "This section of the building had a floor and a ceiling and very little in between that the eye could use.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_xenograft, first_xenograft_1, "A piece of some other architecture seemed to have taken root in the floor plan.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_xenograft, first_xenograft_2, "The building changed its handwriting here, halfway through a sentence.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_xenograft, first_xenograft_3, "This patch of architecture looked like a transplant. The building had grown around the join.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_xenograft, first_xenograft_4, "An unfamiliar piece of building sat inside a familiar one. Neither quite explained the other.")
DISPATCH_LINE(first_xenograft, first_xenograft_5, "Somewhere behind the plans for this place was another set of plans. A piece had slipped through.")
DISPATCH_LINE(route_return, route_return_1, "The route came back through familiar ground. For once the building could supply a reference.")
DISPATCH_LINE(route_return, route_return_2, "Here was a section the runner had crossed before. It felt almost like an acquaintance.")
DISPATCH_LINE(route_return, route_return_3, "The runner had seen this part earlier. A place could be worth remembering without being worth keeping.")
DISPATCH_LINE(route_return, route_return_4, "A familiar patch of floor turned up again after the intervening rooms.")
DISPATCH_LINE(route_return, route_return_5, "This stretch had a past now. The runner had given it one on the way through.")
DISPATCH_LINE(pause_to_listen, pause_to_listen_1, "After all that walking, the runner stopped. The building could have the next word.")
DISPATCH_LINE(pause_to_listen, pause_to_listen_2, "A pause put a little space between one footstep and the next.")
DISPATCH_LINE(pause_to_listen, pause_to_listen_3, "For a moment the runner stood still. Distance could wait.")
DISPATCH_LINE(pause_to_listen, pause_to_listen_4, "Without another step to mark the time, the moment seemed rather longer.")
DISPATCH_LINE(pause_to_listen, pause_to_listen_5, "The runner stopped awhile. For once, nothing on the floor plan needed an immediate answer.")
DISPATCH_LINE(dark_walk, dark_walk_1, "The runner walked with the flashlight off. For a while the battery had nothing to do.")
DISPATCH_LINE(dark_walk, dark_walk_2, "With the lamp switched off, the runner's progress drew no charge at all.")
DISPATCH_LINE(dark_walk, dark_walk_3, "The scavenger kept moving without a beam to announce the way.")
DISPATCH_LINE(dark_walk, dark_walk_4, "For this stretch, the flashlight rode along as luggage.")
DISPATCH_LINE(dark_walk, dark_walk_5, "The runner went on by whatever light the building provided.")
DISPATCH_LINE(far_from_rig, far_from_rig_1, "Forty-five meters out, the rig was becoming a destination again.")
DISPATCH_LINE(far_from_rig, far_from_rig_2, "The runner had put some distance between salvage and shelter. The return trip was part of the price.")
DISPATCH_LINE(far_from_rig, far_from_rig_3, "From this far out, a place on the rig's couch was worth the walk back.")
DISPATCH_LINE(far_from_rig, far_from_rig_4, "The rig lay well away now. Its advantage as a refuge depended on getting back to it.")
DISPATCH_LINE(far_from_rig, far_from_rig_5, "There was work out here, and shelter back there. The distance between them kept the job interesting.")
DISPATCH_LINE(scanner_overheat, scanner_overheat_1, "The scanner had run hot. For a while the scavenger would have to trust ordinary eyes.")
DISPATCH_LINE(scanner_overheat, scanner_overheat_2, "Heat had put an end to the reading. The scanner needed time to cool.")
DISPATCH_LINE(scanner_overheat, scanner_overheat_3, "The instrument had found its own limit before the runner found the building's.")
DISPATCH_LINE(scanner_overheat, scanner_overheat_4, "A hot scanner was another thing to carry. Its useful life would resume once it cooled.")
DISPATCH_LINE(scanner_overheat, scanner_overheat_5, "The runner's electronic eye had overheated. The walls could keep their secrets for the moment.")
DISPATCH_LINE(scanner_cooled, scanner_cooled_1, "The scanner had cooled enough for another look through the walls.")
DISPATCH_LINE(scanner_cooled, scanner_cooled_2, "The instrument was ready again. The scavenger had their electronic eye back.")
DISPATCH_LINE(scanner_cooled, scanner_cooled_3, "Enough heat had bled away. Another scan was possible.")
DISPATCH_LINE(scanner_cooled, scanner_cooled_4, "The scanner's rest had paid off. It could earn its place in the load again.")
DISPATCH_LINE(scanner_cooled, scanner_cooled_5, "At last, the scanner could offer more than the warmth of its casing.")
DISPATCH_LINE(floor_blackout, floor_blackout_1, "The floor lights went out. The runner's own lamp had suddenly become a much better investment.")
DISPATCH_LINE(floor_blackout, floor_blackout_2, "Darkness spread through the floor as the building lights failed.")
DISPATCH_LINE(floor_blackout, floor_blackout_3, "The lamps went out together. Even a bad office could be efficient about some things.")
DISPATCH_LINE(floor_blackout, floor_blackout_4, "A blackout took the building lights. What remained was a different sort of floor plan.")
DISPATCH_LINE(floor_blackout, floor_blackout_5, "Without its overhead lights, the floor lost a good deal of its ordinary office manners.")
DISPATCH_LINE(lights_return, lights_return_1, "The floor lights came back. Shapes in the building had edges again.")
DISPATCH_LINE(lights_return, lights_return_2, "The blackout lifted. A little ordinary office lighting went a very long way.")
DISPATCH_LINE(lights_return, lights_return_3, "Power returned to the floor. The runner had their share of the light again.")
DISPATCH_LINE(lights_return, lights_return_4, "The building switched its lamps back on as if the interruption had been perfectly routine.")
DISPATCH_LINE(lights_return, lights_return_5, "The darkness loosened its hold on the floor. The overhead lights were back.")
DISPATCH_LINE(charger_ready, charger_ready_1, "A fresh battery was ready on the rig. The charger had finished its quiet work.")
DISPATCH_LINE(charger_ready, charger_ready_2, "Back in the cabin, the charger had a spare cell waiting.")
DISPATCH_LINE(charger_ready, charger_ready_3, "The rig could now supply a battery. One small part of the shift had gone to plan.")
DISPATCH_LINE(charger_ready, charger_ready_4, "There was a charged cell to be had aboard the rig. A useful thing to come home to.")
DISPATCH_LINE(charger_ready, charger_ready_5, "The cabin charger had finished. Its next customer would get a full battery.")
DISPATCH_LINE(reserve_spent, reserve_spent_1, "The reserve finally ran out. The broken rig could no longer keep the cabin safe.")
DISPATCH_LINE(reserve_spent, reserve_spent_2, "The spare power was gone. Even the break room had lost its protection.")
DISPATCH_LINE(reserve_spent, reserve_spent_3, "The last of the reserve went with the cabin lamp. The rig still needed repair.")
DISPATCH_LINE(reserve_spent, reserve_spent_4, "The rig's spare supply was meant to buy time. That time had been spent.")
DISPATCH_LINE(reserve_spent, reserve_spent_5, "The reserve had carried the break room as far as it could. No more shelter until the repair.")
DISPATCH_LINE(floor_descent, floor_descent_1, "One floor deeper. Overhead, the rig had made its own entrance.")
DISPATCH_LINE(floor_descent, floor_descent_2, "The crew's former floor was now the ceiling over their heads.")
DISPATCH_LINE(floor_descent, floor_descent_3, "The descent was over. Whatever this floor held, the runner had a new quota to meet.")
DISPATCH_LINE(floor_descent, floor_descent_4, "Another level settled around the rig. The salvage ledger began again.")
DISPATCH_LINE(floor_descent, floor_descent_5, "The runner had reached the floor below. The building had plenty more of itself to offer.")
